From 26856a67b564d2824b19492361defeae0a412497 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Victor=20Pal=C3=A9ologue?= <victor.paleologue@semio.ai>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:21:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(arora-hal-naoqi): NAO and Pepper as Arora devices over
 libqi-rs-vibe

A NAOqi HAL in pure Rust: it connects to a robot's NAOqi through the `qi`
crate of libqi-rs-vibe (no C++ SDK, no cross-compilation) and exposes
joints, battery, inertial unit, sonars and touch sensors as keys, and
drives joint targets, stiffness, speech, LEDs and the base velocity
through ALMotion, ALTextToSpeech and ALLeds. Tested against an
in-process fake NAOqi built with the same crate, and with a probe
example against naoqi-sim.

libqi-rs-vibe is not on crates.io yet, so the dependency is pinned to a
commit of its repository.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
